# Gate 0 closure — changes to the recovered prototype
#
# Apply to the as-recovered source to reproduce the state in which all 163
# tests pass:
#
#     cd <worktree>/titlepipe
#     git apply --unsafe-paths --directory . ../../gate0-closure.patch
#     # or: patch -p1 < gate0-closure.patch
#
# The frozen archive at %LOCALAPPDATA%\TitlePipe\gate0-prototype-archive stays
# as-recovered and hash-verified against GATE_0_ARCHIVE_MANIFEST.md. This patch
# is the delta, kept in VCS so the closure is not machine-local.
#
# Four changes, each with its reason in the code:
#
#   seed.py       _docx_text falls back to python-docx when pandoc is absent.
#                 pandoc was the only reader, so a missing system binary made
#                 two orders silently vanish from the seed — indistinguishable
#                 from a missing report.
#
#   assemble.py   build_report retains the pre-suppression mortgage set. Without
#                 it the report shows only survivors and v14 cannot tell a lien
#                 released from one dropped by chain termination — the single
#                 distinction R15 turns on.
#
#   validators.py v14_liens_survive_chain_termination, the assertion R15
#                 mandated and Gate 0 found missing. Added to HARD_VALIDATORS.
#                 Fails closed when it cannot see the pre-suppression set.
#
#   test_seed.py  TITLEPIPE_SEED_ROOT makes the delivered-report root
#                 configurable. It defaulted to /mnt/user-data, a path in the
#                 sandbox the prototype was written in.
#
# Contains no client-derived party names, addresses or amounts.
#
